{
  "duration": 86.519,
  "phrases": [
    {
      "start": 0.099,
      "end": 1.059,
      "text": "So welcome back again."
    },
    {
      "start": 1.439,
      "end": 2.519,
      "text": "Time for one more problem."
    },
    {
      "start": 3.059,
      "end": 8.079,
      "text": "Now, in this problem, we are given that a runner maintains a speed of six meter per second for 12 minutes."
    },
    {
      "start": 8.479,
      "end": 9.139,
      "text": "The question is"
    },
    {
      "start": 9.659,
      "end": 12.779,
      "text": "asking us to find the total distance covered by the runner."
    },
    {
      "start": 13.34,
      "end": 13.799,
      "text": "Now, first,"
    },
    {
      "start": 14.179,
      "end": 15.779,
      "text": "let us note down the given values."
    },
    {
      "start": 16.379,
      "end": 18.579,
      "text": "Speed of the runner is six meter per second."
    },
    {
      "start": 19.139,
      "end": 20.519,
      "text": "Time taken is 12 minutes."
    },
    {
      "start": 21.0,
      "end": 22.279,
      "text": "Be very sure about one thing."
    },
    {
      "start": 22.799,
      "end": 25.239,
      "text": "The speed is given in meter per second,"
    },
    {
      "start": 25.859,
      "end": 28.139,
      "text": "but the time is given in minutes."
    },
    {
      "start": 28.76,
      "end": 30.159,
      "text": "So before using the formula,"
    },
    {
      "start": 30.739,
      "end": 33.439,
      "text": "we must first convert the time into seconds."
    },
    {
      "start": 34.0,
      "end": 36.219,
      "text": "We know that one minute is equal to"
    },
    {
      "start": 36.559,
      "end": 37.2,
      "text": "60 seconds,"
    },
    {
      "start": 37.819,
      "end": 40.2,
      "text": "so 12 minutes is equal to 12 into"
    },
    {
      "start": 40.559,
      "end": 40.799,
      "text": "60."
    },
    {
      "start": 41.279,
      "end": 42.419,
      "text": "That gives us"
    },
    {
      "start": 42.84,
      "end": 44.139,
      "text": "720 seconds."
    },
    {
      "start": 44.7,
      "end": 47.699,
      "text": "Now that the units are the same, we can use the formula,"
    },
    {
      "start": 48.239,
      "end": 50.919,
      "text": "distance is equal to speed into time."
    },
    {
      "start": 51.36,
      "end": 52.319,
      "text": "Putting the values,"
    },
    {
      "start": 52.68,
      "end": 54.84,
      "text": "distance is equal to six into"
    },
    {
      "start": 55.279,
      "end": 58.739,
      "text": "720. After multiplying this, we get"
    },
    {
      "start": 59.139,
      "end": 60.739,
      "text": "4,320"
    },
    {
      "start": 61.319,
      "end": 61.84,
      "text": "meter."
    },
    {
      "start": 62.34,
      "end": 68.76,
      "text": "Now that we have found the distance in meters, let us convert it into kilometer because all the options are given in kilometer."
    },
    {
      "start": 69.199,
      "end": 70.159,
      "text": "We know that"
    },
    {
      "start": 70.5,
      "end": 73.019,
      "text": "1000 meter is equal to one kilometer."
    },
    {
      "start": 73.479,
      "end": 75.779,
      "text": "So 4,320 divided by"
    },
    {
      "start": 76.099,
      "end": 79.099,
      "text": "1000 is equal to 4.32 kilometer."
    },
    {
      "start": 79.699,
      "end": 82.639,
      "text": "So the runner covers 4.32 kilometer."
    },
    {
      "start": 83.18,
      "end": 83.559,
      "text": "Hence,"
    },
    {
      "start": 84.139,
      "end": 86.519,
      "text": "the correct answer is option B."
    }
  ],
